{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked tests cover each obligation in `judge.rendering`.\n\n**1. Inputs are presented through `NodeContents::format`.**\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` sets a custom formatter that returns `formatted input: …`. It asserts the first user message contains `formatted input: source`. The raw contents are only `source`, so the text can only come from `format`.\n- `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` checks the order of the delivered contents for queued inputs.\n- `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks the contents delivered for queued inputs, including repeated and successor inputs.\n- On the `read_node` path, `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` uses the `distinct_pages` formatter. The `ParallelConversations` provider asserts the delivered page contains `ALPHA-CONTENTS` or `BETA-CONTENTS`. Those strings come only from the formatter, so the tool delivers `format` output.\n- `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` in `src/sdk.rs` checks the habeas `HabeasNodeContent::format`.\n\n**2. Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n- `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` changes the underlying contents after the read. It asserts `format()` still returns `before` and `fingerprint()` still equals the snapshot fingerprint. It also asserts only one read happened.\n- `default_tool_…` asserts the recorded dependency fingerprint is `source` while the text is the formatted string, with exactly one read.\n- This also covers \"formatting uses the retained value with no further reads or fallible preparation\".\n\n**3. Queued-input failures return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n- `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` covers three failures:\n  - a read failure, which returns `Graph(\"read\")`;\n  - an edges failure, which returns `Graph(\"edges\")`;\n  - a preparation (render) failure, which returns `Graph(\"render\")`.\n- It also asserts that no dependencies are recorded and that no agent request is made for the failed render.\n\n**4. Failures during `read_node` come back as a tool error and the agent can recover.**\n- `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes the formatter fail during `Domain::node_content`.\n- It asserts the next request carries a single error `ToolResult` for `read_node` with the message `unsupported node contents`.\n- The conversation then continues to a successful `submit_result`, and no dependencies are recorded.\n\nOther tests exercise `read_node` success text and page snapshots, such as `a_complete_node_read_has_text_and_no_continuation`, but are not marked for this requirement. They are not needed here, because the marked tests already cover the obligations.\n\nThe cited `node_content` and `node_content.format` requirements are context, and their tests are not reassessed. No gaps are found, and there are no acknowledgments to account for.",
  "references": "f6ca580b7ad3955509357366e0e56b0d72b32452bd72e328b9bd2bf30481a0de",
